The tester's 49809, trio 1: request_introduction was refused twice with
„route looks closed" (§110.1), and then the unsent-instruction guard
(44367) replaced the reply with „კითხვა არ გაიგზავნა. გთხოვ, თხოვნა კიდევ
ერთხელ მომწერე." — an invitation to retry the very route that is closed.
Trio 2, where the guard did not fire, read the §110.1 line and another way.

A run whose request_introduction came back with reason route_closed is now
never taken for an instruction left unsent: the refusal was the server's
own decision, and the reply the model wrote under §110.1 stands. No new text
reaches anyone; the guard simply does not overwrite.

Not in this change: running the closed-route check before the plan names
the bridge (trio 1 saw the plan card first). That moves the check into plan
building and is a day item.

DONE WHEN: a closed-route refusal ends with the §110.1 line and another
way, never the generic not-sent line, in 2 of 2 trios.

